6
7 "Section 2.
8
9 (a) There is appropriated five hundred thousand dollars
10 ($500,000.00) from the general fund to the University of Wyoming
11 center for blockchain and digital innovation. Funds from this
12 general fund appropriation shall be expended by the University of
13 Wyoming center for blockchain and digital innovation to develop
14 software for the secretary of state's office that would allow for
15 online filing of initial business entity formation and amendments,
16 notary registration and renewal, apostille or authentication
17 certification requests, lobbyist registration and renewal and all
18 initial and additional filing types, as well as amendments. This
19 appropriation shall be for the period beginning with the effective
20 date of this act and ending June 30, 2026. This appropriation shall
21 not be transferred or expended for any other purpose and any
22 unexpended, unobligated funds remaining from this appropriation
23 shall revert as provided by law on June 30, 2026. It is the intent
24 of the legislature that this appropriation not be included in the
25 University of Wyoming's standard budget for the immediately
26 succeeding fiscal biennium.
27
28 (b) If 2025 Senate File 0001, 2025 House Bill 0001 or 2025
29 Senate File 0095 is enacted into law, the appropriation in
30 subsection (a) of this section shall be reduced by one dollar
31 ($1.00) for every one dollar ($1.00) appropriated to the University
32 of Wyoming center for blockchain and digital innovation for the
33 same or substantially similar purposes as specified in subsection
34 (a) of this section in 2025 Senate File 0001, 2025 House Bill 0001
35 or 2025 Senate File 0095.". DRISKILL
